{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>ונשאו</b> — The word ומסרפו has no [grammatical] parallel. And Rabbi Judah ben Koreish said: כי דודו is his father's brother and מסרפו his mother's brother, and this is reasoning without proof. And the one who says that its meaning is 'the one who saves him from the burning' will exchange the samekh for shin, but we have not seen this pattern on the intensive binyan with dagesh, except in a pejorative sense, as in: שרשך מסעף פארה. Now the meaning is that people enter a house to see who has died of plague, or that the house collapsed on them because the earth quakes, as I have mentioned, and likewise after it, 'and the great house is struck.' And behold, a dod, one of the people who were in the house, will come to take the dead out of the house to the graves and to carry the living from there, and when the man recognizes his kinsman and carries him, he will say to the one in the innermost part of the house, 'Is there still anyone there?' — he will reply, saying, 'Hush,' do not say this and do not let your voice be heard, lest the heart of the hearers weaken, and not one of them justifies the name of Heaven, to mention the honored Name."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Resolved הזכרתי as Ibn Ezra's cross-reference to his own earlier comment on this passage or its context."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:25.404538257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}